% A program may define a type whose NAME an exposed module also defines at a
% DIFFERENT ARITY.  NetMsg/1 here and NetMsg/0 in programs/system/mad_predicates.glp
% are two type constructors, not two spellings of one, and mad_predicates is in
% every program (the root self.glp -expose's it), so this is not a contrived
% pairing: it is what programs/spm/{cva,gsg,secure_gsg} do, and what stopped all
% three loading.  The linked program's type definitions used to be keyed by bare
% name, so whichever arity the directory walk reached second was dropped and every
% reference to it failed to resolve — here mad_predicates.glp:19's NetStream would
% lose its element type.  GREEN, and it must stay green whichever order the walk
% reaches the two definitions in.
NetMsg(C) ::= wrap(C).
NetMsgList(C) ::= [] ; [NetMsg(C) | NetMsgList(C)].
imported procedure code#go(NetMsgList(Constant)?).
exported procedure go(NetMsgList(Constant)?).
go(X) :- code # go(X?).
